# C - exp(2.5e13 y) from rest (the review's row): the continuation's answer, bit for bit (its
# distance to the 80-digit root and its count are in the group above).
# [measured: this group's own assertions, roots from a 60-digit continuation oracle, NUM3 tree, 2026-10-31]
var _n3o_xt, _n3o_xv = ode_bdf2_checked(&_n41r_ex, F64_HALF, 0, 0, 0x3F50624DD2F1A9FC, 0x3DDB7CDFD9D7BDBB, &_n3o_o);
assert_eq(_n3o_o, 0xBCF7862299ADB5BB, "bdf2: C - exp(2.5e13 y) from rest -> 0xBCF7862299ADB5BB");
# Newton's steps keep their bits and count: Van der Pol mu = 10, backward Euler, max_newton 50,
# is 3.4.0's 0x3FC1CE9C3DE75D42 in 6 evaluations. With max_newton 1 Newton stops after 4 (3.4.0:
# NO_CONVERGENCE) and the continuation's one increment reaches the root: 0x3FC1CE9C3DE75160, 3,042
